We can display the contrast Sandel is drawing in the organ case as follows: $\begin{aligned}
\text{Do not use the patient}
&\Longrightarrow \text{avoid bad} \\
&\quad \text{long-run consequences}, \\
\text{Do not use the patient}
&\Longrightarrow \text{respect the person} \\
&\quad \text{as an individual}.\end{aligned}$ The lecture’s question is whether the first line can ever be enough by itself.

