p.src:
At this point Sandel makes the decisive escalation. Joe had called redistribution theft. Nozick, we are told, goes one step further. Taxation does not merely take an external object. It takes earnings, and earnings are the fruits of labor. The argument therefore unfolds in a chain: $\begin{aligned}
\text{taxation of earnings}
&\to \text{taking fruits of labor} \\
&\to \text{claim on labor} \\
&\to \text{forced labor} \\
&\to \text{slavery}.\end{aligned}$

